+## Voyage 2 — Browser acceptance defect fix
+
+**Base commit:** v1-qm (10da9e8).
+
+**Two product defects identified** from fixed external browser acceptance suite:
+
+### Defect A: List re-render destroys DOM identity (failures 1-4)
+`render()` does `dom.todoList.innerHTML = ''` and rebuilds all `<li>` elements from scratch on every toggle action. In a real browser, Cypress holds live DOM references to `<li>` elements; replacing them causes "element detached from DOM" errors. The app MUST mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place when toggling completion state (update class and checkbox attribute), not rebuild the list.
+
+### Defect B: Escape key does not cancel edit (failure 5)
+The blur handler uses capture phase (`addEventListener('blur', ..., true)`), so it fires before the keydown handler completes. When Escape is pressed: blur fires first, calling `editTodo(id, e.target.value)` which overwrites the todo title with the edited text; then the keydown handler sets `editingId = null` and calls `render()`, but the model data is already corrupted. Fix: track an `editCancelled` flag; set it in the Escape keydown handler; clear it at end of keydown handler; check it in the blur handler to skip saving when true.
+
+**New specs written:**
+- `specs/dom-identity.feature` — 2 scenarios pinning DOM node preservation on toggle
+- `specs/edit-cancel.feature` — 1 scenario pinning Escape restores original title
+
+**Updated watchbill:** 3 new scenarios added to watch1.
